<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Édouard Brémond</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Édouard Brémond was a French army officer. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> he led the French military mission to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a>, which supported the Arab Revolt, and from 1919 to 1920 he was chief administrator of the French-occupied zone of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, relying partly on the Armenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a>. Turkish nationalist resistance forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to agree to leave the region in 1921.</p></div>
